   theme.
 - Presentation lowers raster surfaces into ASCII, ANSI16, ANSI256, or
   true-color output.
+- ANSI256 text presentation preserves the existing named-color mappings for
+  black, red, green, yellow, blue, magenta, cyan, white, and gray. Other colors
+  are gamut-clamped and matched against the conventional extended palette at
+  indices 16–255 using squared distance between encoded RGB channels, choosing
+  the lower index on ties. Terminals can customize this palette; matching does
+  not promise perceptual similarity or measured contrast. ANSI16 conversion,
+  true-color output, and capability detection retain their existing behavior.
 - Presentation sanitizes authored text and OSC 8 hyperlink destinations before
   it emits terminal bytes. Layout, semantics, and raster artifacts do not
   encode terminal-control safety rules.
